 > Ok, here is one for the dev team...
 > I would love to run nethack under windows 3.0 in a dos window.
 > (I like to come back and forth without having to save - Yes, I am lazy)
 > When I try to run it, it tells me that the application has violated 
 > system integrity and I should reboot. Is this a bug, or is it one of
 > the options I have set, or is it the overlay manager (my first thought)?
 > 
 > Thanks in advance.
Running nethack under windows works fine, but you have to set up 
your machine so that it doesn't provide any expanded memory.  Nethack
uses any available expanded memory to minimize disk swapping, but for
some reason this doesn't work under windows.  I have seen this happen with other
ems programs too, so it may be a windows bug.
If you have the emm386.sys driver in config.sys, try to use the parameter "noems".
It will still be possible to load programs high.
If you want to have the ems support, try a .pif file wich spesifies
no ems memory for nethack.  
